body:
## Problem

PR-B transfers deterministic TypeScript/product authority, but unit-test execution remains split across root Vitest discovery, package tasks, and exceptional integration/browser lanes. That leaves no fail-closed answer for who owns each repository test file or whether a bounded Buck lane collected exactly the files it claims.

## Decision

- generate a schema-v2 authority bridge for 32 bounded package lanes;
- publish declared Vitest collection artifacts and reconcile them against the filesystem census;
- derive exact source-side complements and explicit integration/Playwright owners from the same registry;
- execute all bounded lanes through one local-only Buck invocation;
- keep dedicated Notion, megarepo, Utils Playwright, and TUI React Playwright boundaries explicit and merge-blocking;
- repair the reactivated TUI browser contracts and keep Node-only stdout modules outside browser evaluation.

The partition is exhaustive and disjoint: 433 repository test files = 282 Buck-owned + 115 generic source complements + 23 explicit source owners + 13 files in source-only packages.

## Evidence

- fresh synthetic collection: 32 artifacts, 282 files, 4,292 tests, 1,171 local actions, 0 remote actions;
- bounded execution: 32 pass, 0 fail; repeat run transferred 0 B;
- baseline gate: all 433 files owned; all 32 collection artifacts exact; all 28 baseline files collected (23 bounded);
- authority decoder/package-tree: 67 tests pass; Buck projection guards: 20 pass; CI required-job parity: 70 pass;
- TUI React Playwright: 19/19; Utils Playwright: 3/3;
- `@overeng/utils-dev:typecheck` and its Buck test lane pass after the review-driven Node-only gate cleanup;
- `genie --check` passes; generated workflow is 468,495 bytes (<500,000); `devenv.nix` parses;
- three final adversarial reviews found two merge-blocking gaps (TUI status not required; relocated gate lacked a viable type boundary); both are fixed and directly re-proved.

Full local Nix realization was intentionally not attempted because the host root filesystem is at its safety threshold. GitHub CI supplies the non-destructive full-system proof.

## Remaining draft gate

Cache-disabled complete local execution passes in 44.3 s, but that is correctness evidence—not BUCK-R07 warm-cache evidence. Before this PR is marked ready, run exact-head GitHub CI and record authenticated complete-surface test-cache reuse, a wiped second context, relevant-edit invalidation causality, and warm/fresh timings.

## Stack

- Base: #1260 (`schickling/2026-09-10-buck2-authority-transfer`)
- This PR: bounded unit-test authority
- Epic: #1147

## Review focus

1. `buck2-test-authority.json.genie.ts` and the runtime decoder must remain independent fail-closed checks.
2. `test:run` must execute every bounded lane exactly once and every source complement through its declared owner.
3. Browser/integration owners intentionally remain outside Buck but are required CI checks.
4. Collection actions are cacheable only with fully declared inputs and no inherited environment.

